==Battleground==
*3 [[Big Sal]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 2.67 seconds<sup>80f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*1 [[Bears Be Back]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bears Be Back's strength magnification here is 4,000%, giving them a hefty 2,000,000 HP and a total of about 14,000 DPS. On top of that, they also have a 33% chance to [[Weaken]], [[Freeze]], [[Slow]], and a 21% chance to [[Knockback]] and [[Warp]], making them very threatening. Despite all of this, they are still very counterable with their many traits. Besides Bears Be Back, the only other major threat is Big Sal. As per most Big Sal stages, [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]], and [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] are recommended. Be careful though, as there are three Big Sals and if any of them reach the [[Cat Base]], it's over.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Sunrise Sirius]]: With immunities to everything Bears Be Back can inflict on top of outranging them, she is a great pick for the stage. Adding onto this, her cooldown is only 78 seconds long, meaning that in the case she dies, another will be ready soon after.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]]: Kasli is a bit tricky to use due to not naturally outranging Bears Be Back, but she's still a great pick for this stage due to her 100% Curse uptime and Weaken Immunity. In addition, the myriad of peons spammed on this stage give her constant stepping stones. [[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blue-Eyed Asuka]] can be used similarly, but she has a worse Curse uptime and lower range, making her an even riskier choice.

==Trivia==
*The missing trigonometric function, tan(gent), is part of Sine-Cosine Mine's Japanese name, Sine-Cosine <u>Tan</u>kō (サインコサイン炭鉱, "Sine-Cosine Coal Mine").
*Sine-Cosine Mine is the first non-event stage since [[The Haunted 1LDK]] to contain an enemy from a monthly event.

